#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1363 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "any-branch 2: an unassigned subject (ARMNRS='NOT ASSIGNED') has an empty ARMCD but a populated ARM -> fires on row 1. RE-PINNED by M2-D25 (exact, case-sensitive CT comparison): the rows carried 'Not Assigned' in mixed case while the Check normalised with upper(); with upper() retired the mixed-case spelling no longer matches the ARMNULRS submission value, so the data now carries the exact term and the any-branch-2 coverage this fixture exists for is preserved. Casing is owned by CT2001."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 ARM="Arm A"
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
col ARMNRS  type=Char label="Reason Arm and/or Actual Arm is Null"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 |  | Arm A | NOT ASSIGNED
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023 |  |       | NOT ASSIGNED
